1. Bare Dark Energy: \( \rho_{\text{DE}}^{\text{bare}} = \sum_{p} \frac{1}{p} \sim \log \log x + M \to \infty \)
2. Renormalized Dark Energy: \( \Lambda_{\text{arith}} = \lim_{x \to \infty} \left( \sum_{p \leq x} \frac{1}{p} - \log \log x \right) = M \approx 0.261497 \)
3. Zeta Regularization: \( \sum_p \frac{1}{p^s} = \log \zeta(s) + \text{analytic} \), and \( \lim_{s \to 1^+} (\log \zeta(s) - \log(s-1)) = M \)

